-- title:
--   Q Bipartite Linear Cons Defect Nonneg Of Right Total One
-- statement:
--   **A complete right submeasurement makes the linear consistency defect nonnegative.**
--
--   Let $\psi$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $A$ and $B$ be submeasurements with a common finite outcome set, and suppose that the total operator of $B$ is the identity:
--
--   $$
--   B_{\mathrm{total}}=I.
--   $$
--
--   For the linear defect
--
--   $$
--   \Lambda_{\psi}(A,B)=\operatorname{ev}_{\psi}(A_{\mathrm{total}}\otimes B_{\mathrm{total}})-\sum_a\operatorname{ev}_{\psi}(A_a\otimes B_a),
--   $$
--
--   one has
--
--   $$
--   0\le\Lambda_{\psi}(A,B).
--   $$
--
--   The proof bounds the matching mass by the expectation of the left total operator, which equals the total overlap because the right total is $I$. Consequently the ordinary bipartite consistency defect, defined as the positive part of $\Lambda_{\psi}$, equals the linear defect in this setting. This nonnegativity is used to pass from averaged linear defects to averaged consistency errors.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.qBipartiteLinearConsDefect_nonneg_of_right_total_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
